 so defection is the unique fixed point under this reading.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at this twin prisoner's dilemma where the two copies see different observations, so under the A-FDT reading in the essay they count as different decision nodes. That means the other copy's action is held fixed at its prior, and sending comes out dominant in my payoff table either way.\n\nI'm weighing whether the other copy really counts as a separate decision node, since the essay's heuristic says a different input means a different node. Taking that literally, the other copy's action stays fixed, and sending still dominates, so defection is the unique fixed point under this reading.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10182,"completion_tokens":717,"total_tokens":10899,"cost":0.055068,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055068,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040728,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01434},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":317,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}